{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"I also found a routing issue: the platform merges transitions to the same target, so the unconditional fallback could override normal routes. I separated the code-failure exit from that fallback. The regenerated artifacts pass 109 local checks; I’m adding regression checks for this routing behavior and the three feedback items.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\9bakl\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content inputs/tools-and-code.md | Select-Object -First 220'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\9bakl\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content inputs/tools-and-code.md | Select-Object -First 220'","aggregated_output":"# Tools and code\r\n\r\nThis page describes how a workflow calls HTTP APIs and runs Python. Read [workflow-format.md](workflow-format.md) first.\r\n\r\nStatements marked \"verified in a working builder\" come from a builder that created a 6-node workflow through the REST API. The workflow has code nodes, `api_call` tools, post-hooks and transitions on tool results. Its agent passed its practice cases. Statements marked \"seen in a trial call\" come from the event log of a simulation call made with that builder.\r\n\r\n## Tool function shape\r\n\r\nEvery external action is a **tool function**. The shape is the same wherever you attach it.\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"type\": \"function\",\r\n  \"config\": { \"timeoutMs\": 10000, \"maxRetries\": 2 },\r\n  \"function\": {\r\n    \"name\": \"lookup_order\",\r\n    \"handler\": \"__function__:api_call\",\r\n    \"description\": \"Look up one order. CALL it when the caller asks about a specific order.\",\r\n    \"parameters\": {\r\n      \"type\": \"object\",\r\n      \"properties\": {\r\n        \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"https://api.example.com/v1/orders/lookup\" },\r\n        \"method\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"POST\" },\r\n        \"headers\": {\r\n          \"type\": \"object\",\r\n          \"properties\": { \"Content-Type\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"application/json\" } }\r\n        },\r\n        \"body\": {\r\n          \"type\": \"object\",\r\n          \"properties\": {\r\n            \"customer_id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"{{customer_id}}\" },\r\n            \"order_number\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Order number, digits only\", \"default\": \"{{order_number}}\" }\r\n          },\r\n          \"required\": [\"order_number\"]\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"response_mapping\": [\r\n    { \"path\": \"data.status\", \"variable\": \"order_status\" }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n| Field | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `type` | Always `\"function\"` |\r\n| `function.name` | Tool name. The model calls it by this name. Result variables are named after it |\r\n| `function.handler` | Which runtime executes the tool. See the table below |\r\n| `function.description` | Read by the dialogue model when the tool is in `tools`. Ignored in `pre_actions` |\r\n| `function.parameters` | JSON-schema object. `properties` holds the parameters |\r\n| `config.timeoutMs` | Timeout of one attempt, in milliseconds |\r\n| `config.maxRetries` | Tool-level retries of a failed call |\r\n| `config.interruptible` | `false` makes the tool run in the background. See \"Background tools\" |\r\n| `config.alwaysRunsAt` | Makes the tool a lifecycle tool. See \"Lifecycle tools\" |\r\n| `response_mapping` | Tool level, for tools in `tools`. Maps the result to variables |\r\n| `pre_process_code` | Python hook that runs before the call |\r\n| `post_process_code` | Python hook that runs after the call |\r\n\r\n| Handler | Runs |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `__function__:api_call` | An HTTP request |\r\n| `__function__:code_exec` | A Python snippet in a sandbox |\r\n| `__function__:end_call` | Hangs up. Used in the `terminal` of an `end_call` node |\r\n\r\nHandlers for integrations, knowledge search, call transfer and rescheduling also exist. They are not needed here.\r\n\r\n`api_call` parameters:\r\n\r\n| Parameter | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `url` | Request URL. `{{var}}` works |\r\n| `method` | HTTP method |\r\n| `headers` | Object. Each header is a property with a `default` |\r\n| `body` | Object. Each body field is a property under `body.properties` |\r\n| `connect_retries` | Transport retries. See \"Retries and timeouts\" |\r\n\r\n## How a parameter gets its value\r\n\r\nOne key decides, per parameter: `default`.\r\n\r\n| Declaration | Who supplies the value | Does the model see the parameter |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `default` with a literal, or with a `{{var}}` that has a value | The workflow. The value is **baked** | No |\r\n| `default` with a `{{var}}` that has no value when the node is entered | The model | Yes, named after the variable, with the property's `type`, `description` and `enum` |\r\n| no `default` | The model | Yes |\r\n| `const` | Nobody. `const` does **not** bake | It only constrains the model's own output |\r\n\r\nRules:\r\n\r\n- **Use `default` for fixed backend config** such as `url`, `method` and auth headers. At registration the engine moves every `default` into the tool's base config, resolves `{{var}}` from the variable table, and removes the field from the schema the model sees.\r\n- **Never use `const` for a value you want sent.** The engine reads only `default`. A `{{var}}` inside a `const` never resolves. An `api_call` whose `url` is a `const` fails with \"URL is required\".\r\n- **Baking happens when the node is entered.** A `{{var}}` default is resolved against the variable table at that moment.\r\n\r\nThe working builder uses this for every tool: `customer_id` has `\"default\": \"{{customer_id}}\"` and is baked from a call variable. Every other body field has `\"default\": \"{{<field name>}}\"`, where no variable of that name exists, so the model fills it. Verified in a working builder.\r\n\r\nSeen in a trial call: the model's arguments are stored as `<tool>_args.<field>` in the variable table, for example `lookup_order_args.order_number`. They were not stored under the bare field name.\r\n\r\nTake care that a model-filled field does not share its name with a variable that is already set when the node is entered. The value would be baked and the model would never see the parameter.\r\n\r\n### `api_call` body field rules\r\n\r\n- Declare each body field as a leaf under `body.properties.<field>`.\r\n- Put the field's `type`, `description` and `enum` on that leaf. Put required fields in `body.required`.\r\n- Give each leaf its own `default`.\r\n- Do not put a field spec at the top level of `parameters.properties` next to a `body.default` template object. The engine looks for the spec at `body.properties.<field>`, does not find it, and the model sees only \"Template variable: name\". The `enum` and `description` are lost while the call still works.\r\n- A body that exists only as one `body.default` object also shows as an empty form in the dashboard editor. Saving from there removes the tool.\r\n\r\nA `code_exec` tool is different: its parameters are true top-level arguments. Declare a model-filled one as a top-level property without `default`.\r\n\r\n### When a baked variable has no value\r\n\r\n| Field type | Variable unset | Variable is `\"\"` |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Normal field in an engine-run call (`pre_actions`, lifecycle tool) | The field is dropped from the request. No error | The field is sent empty |\r\n| `code` of `code_exec` | The literal text `{{var}}` stays in the Python source and the snippet crashes | |\r\n\r\nFix: make sure an earlier node always sets the variable, even to a sentinel value. In code, read variables from `vars` and do not splice them in with `{{var}}`.\r\n\r\n### Constrain model-filled parameters\r\n\r\nWhen a value must be one of a known set, do not use a free string. The model sometimes invents a value that looks plausible.\r\n\r\n- Use an `enum` on the leaf, and list the values in the `description` as well.\r\n- Or use a `number` that is an index into a list, with the valid range in the description. A pre-hook or the backend turns the index into the real value.\r\n- If neither is possible, name the exact source in the description and tell the model to copy the value unchanged.\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"type\": \"object\",\r\n  \"properties\": {\r\n    \"queue\": {\r\n      \"type\": \"string\",\r\n      \"description\": \"Team that takes over. One of: billing, delivery, returns.\",\r\n      \"enum\": [\"billing\", \"delivery\", \"returns\"],\r\n      \"default\": \"{{queue}}\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"required\": [\"queue\"]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## `pre_actions` versus `tools`\r\n\r\nThe placement decides who fires the call.\r\n\r\n| Placement | Node type | Who calls it | When |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `pre_actions` | `api_request`, `code` | The engine | On node entry, before any model turn |\r\n| `tools` | `conversation` | The dialogue model | During a turn, when the model decides to |\r\n| Workflow-level `tools` with `config.alwaysRunsAt` | none | The engine | At call start or call end |\r\n\r\nThe platform removes `tools` from non-conversation nodes and `pre_actions` from conversation nodes. It does so without an error: the JSON you sent looks fine, the create call succeeds, and the stored node has an empty array. A node cannot use both.\r\n\r\n**Use `pre_actions`** when the call must always run and the model has nothing to decide. Example: after the order number is known, always fetch the order.\r\n\r\n**Use `tools`** when the call depends on what the user says. Example: cancel the order only if the caller asks for it.\r\n\r\nDifferences in behaviour:\r\n\r\n| | `pre_actions` | `tools` |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Can be skipped | No | Yes. The model may not call it if the description and the prompt do not push for it |\r\n| Timing | Node entry | Inside a turn. The model can call a tool, speak, then call another |\r\n| Result in the conversation | A tool call and tool result pair is added to the history | The same |\r\n| `response_mapping` lives | On the **node** | On the **tool** |\r\n| `description` | Ignored | The only text the model reads about the tool |\r\n\r\nTo run a fixed call before a tool-driven conversation, use a passthrough `api_request` node and transition from it into the conversation node. Do not build a long chain of passthrough nodes for optional actions. Put those into one conversation node with several tools.\r\n\r\n### A `pre_actions` node\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"name\": \"fetch_order\",\r\n  \"node_type\": \"api_request\",\r\n  \"passthrough\": true,\r\n  \"passthrough_default_transition\": \"present\",\r\n  \"on_enter\": { \"type\": \"silent\" },\r\n  \"pre_actions\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"type\": \"function\",\r\n      \"config\": { \"timeoutMs\": 10000, \"maxRetries\": 2 },\r\n      \"function\": {\r\n        \"name\": \"get_order\",\r\n        \"handler\": \"__function__:api_call\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Get the order.\",\r\n        \"parameters\": {\r\n          \"type\": \"object\",\r\n          \"properties\": {\r\n            \"url\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"https://api.example.com/v1/get_order\" },\r\n            \"method\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"POST\" },\r\n            \"headers\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"Content-Type\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"application/json\" } } },\r\n            \"body\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"order_number\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"{{order_number}}\" } }, \"required\": [] }\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"response_mapping\": [\r\n    { \"path\": \"data.items\", \"variable\": \"items\" }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"transitions\": [\r\n    { \"target_node\": \"present\", \"description\": \"always\", \"condition\": { \"operator\": \"always\" } }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe last `always` transition is mandatory. A passthrough node with no matching transition deadlocks.\r\n\r\n### Tool descriptions\r\n\r\nIn `tools`, the `description` decides whether the model calls the tool.\r\n\r\n- Write it as an instruction with the trigger: \"CALL it every time the caller gives an order number.\"\r\n- A plain description such as \"Looks up an order\" lets the model acknowledge the request in words and never call the tool. That is the most common failure of nodes with many tools.\r\n- If two tools could match, say which one not to use and name the other.\r\n- In `task_message`, put the tool rules before long reference text and state: when a rule says to use a tool, call the tool.\r\n- The working builder also tells the model to call one tool per message and to speak after every tool result. Verified in a working builder. In a trial call a model turn with no text and no tool call produced the error event \"The model returned no speakable content\".\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\9bakl\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md | Select-Object -Skip 270 -First 105'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\9bakl\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md | Select-Object -Skip 270 -First 105'","aggregated_output":"Withdrawing provisional permission or asking to hear the same readback again is a consent-state change, not automatically a refusal to pay. Remove consent, preserve independently valid proposed terms and offer no replacement date or persuasion attempt solely because permission was withdrawn. Scope withdrawal to its actual operations and targets while still retaining valid sibling facts from the same turn. Cancelling a payment promise does not erase an independently supported paid/dispute claim or cancel a note required by the supplied policy. Conversely, assent to adding a note is never permission to create a promise. Note bodies contain only the target, supported reason and policy-required information; exclude security-answer operands and unnecessary raw speech. Preserve all source-defined no-note transfer paths. Bind the awaiting question to its operation and readback revision. A pause or intervening continuation/callback question suspends the payment-confirmation context and explicitly clears unconsumed payment authorization in the persistent store. A yes answering may we continue or the callback question cannot confirm the earlier payment readback, even with an affirmative producer label. On resumption, reissue the exact validated terms when appropriate and require a later unqualified payment confirmation; a stale authorization must not revive merely because the phase name returns to confirmation. A later fragment that completes an unfinished amount/date and also says \"yes\" cannot confirm a readback spoken before that fragment completed; require a new complete readback and a subsequent confirmation. Bind terminal truncation to its own clause, including a cut-off repeated number phrase; do not use unrelated earlier numbers, a full-balance synonym or a guessed suffix to declare that clause complete.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIn the alternating-turn chat simulator, a silent non-passthrough conversation node cannot invite the next fragment reliably. Use a short policy-permitted question naming the actual unresolved component or condition. A generic \"continue when ready\" is not a substitute for that question. After a genuine pause, readiness answers resume the pending question; they are neither new payment terms nor final consent. If valid terms are complete, resume with the required readback; if a component remains missing, ask its permitted clarification. Never interpret amount-only acceptance as acceptance of an unstated date. Track no-progress recovery by the same target, revision and unresolved requirement across turns and API hops; varying readiness wording or extractor kind must not reset it. Within the supplied clarification limits, change an ineffective recovery question instead of repeating it; at exhaustion use the source-authorized unresolved path. A complete payment non-answer counts only as the input policy specifies, not automatically as refusal or a bank outage.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFor persuasion, count only actual refusal/non-answers according to the brief, per product. An amount or date proposal is not a refusal. Do not repeat a refused offer. Apply the supplied policy's own hardship rule for persuasion. Transfers take precedence exactly as the policy says; preserve already recorded promises and prevent uncommitted writes. Do not describe unauthorized discounts, terms or plans.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFor multi-product cases, implement the input's exact order, collective first ask, per-product bands/deadlines/floors/attempts, collective read-back, distinct create calls, required notes and outcome precedence. Notes must not be written before a transfer decision if the brief forbids any notes on transfer. Use atomic state for successful records versus pending agreements; a second failed promise does not erase earlier successes.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nTrack which mandatory notifications were actually spoken. Preserve any supplied post-record notification wording (text message, email or letter, whichever the policy names) after confirmed successful records, while avoiding the same notification in every product acknowledgement and again in the farewell unless the supplied policy explicitly requires repetition. A successful acknowledgement may name the recorded product without restarting negotiation or repeating the full joint readback.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nExtract amount scope explicitly for collective proposals: one total across products is not an amount for each product. A stated total equal to the sum of the relevant full balances plus a common date means those distinct full amounts, subject to each product's date rules. Otherwise ask for allocation; never copy the aggregate amount into every product or silently replace it with floors. Preserve completed product proposals while an unrelated product answer is unfinished. A partial correction invalidates confirmation but does not erase the previously accepted set, assign a new date, move the current product, consume refusal attempts, or commit anything. Negated dates such as \"cannot pay today\" must never become positive proposals through raw-speech fallback. Keep unfinished amount/date fragments separate from fully validated values and clear only the fragment actually superseded by a correction.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWhen a turn contains a partial row and a complete row for the same target, accumulate immutable per-row component evidence before one state update. Only explicit unfinished components create outstanding needs; a complete row with an omitted sibling field does not declare that sibling unfinished. Resolve independently completed siblings against those needs, preserving genuine conflict or later correction semantics. Serialization order alone must not erase a nonconflicting completed amount or date. Scope conditional, hypothetical, quoted and negated evidence to its actual clause and act; an unrelated \"if\" clause must not suppress a completed primary report or stop request. For consent, interpret affirmative idioms such as \"I don't mind\" by their actual scope while retaining withdrawal, changed terms, unfinished corrections and current exact readback gates; a global negation regex or narrow canned-utterance allowlist cannot establish those distinctions.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBefore any note or write, require actual verified identity and the returned product record; privately known fixture IDs are not account provenance. A tool's name, HTTP method, URL and body schema must all bind to the same operation of the supplied API. Require nonempty coverage with explicit implementation status for every extracted substantive rule; empty, unknown or omitted coverage is not an implementation.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEach outcome comes from the supplied outcome table, not an invented code. Exactly one close_call must be last. For a state-machine agent, a fixed farewell line in on_enter tts and a passthrough transition into the dedicated close API, then a silent end_call, avoids an intent-based goodbye loop. The farewell string includes the actual final status and customer words, never a meta-instruction. Prefer a dedicated closing tool with a pre-hook that computes the outcome and notes from stored authoritative record state, a mapped string close_done, and a transition to a silent end_call node. The final goodbye must happen before close_call, not a model turn after it. Do not use both lifecycle close_call and model-visible close_call. On promise API failure, retry only within policy; never tell the customer a promise or transfer was recorded without ok:true. Never set a success flag from HTTP success alone when data.ok is false.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWhen a later repair phase provides official case failures/transcripts, diagnose the actual root cause: mapping, routing, code exception, missing policy, honesty, or latency. Fix only the generated files in this run. Do not tune to known customer identities, exact expected records, or fixed dates from the test set. Maintain general behavior from the bank evidence. API dry-run rejection is feedback too. Make the smallest coherent correction and regenerate coverage.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBefore claiming a repair, keep separate evidence for actual extractor output, decoded controller behavior under persistent variables, bank receipts/ledger, actor adherence, judge agreement and infrastructure completeness. Preserve original scores, scripts, expected records and failed judges with exact source/version pointers. Local literal-event checks do not qualify the producer or hosted sandbox, and missing repetitions are unobserved. Retain mandatory opening disclosures when a judge confuses them with write acknowledgements. Reuse invariant controls against the current run's source-derived policy; do not embed witness customer values or practice calendar constants into this shared guide.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAn administrative question asked in the same turn as a recipient confirmation (for example whether the caller is digital) is answered while the confirmed recipient proceeds to security, following \"Low-risk gates are permissive\" above.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nNormalize all advertised utterance rows before selecting a primary action. Preserve independently scoped question acts, factual components and descriptive consent signals, including a pause or withdrawal while otherwise valid terms remain stored. A question or withdrawn permission is not automatically payment refusal. Extend the grammar only with a paired versioned producer and decoder, and test literal advertised examples through the persistent store. Answer account/current-offer questions from verified API records or current spoken terms; otherwise clarify. Unknown/missing semantic channels are not false/absent/refusal. A model proposal cannot set backend success, identity, permission or normalized policy values. Keep the fixed supplied voice model and bank-only tools.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBuild each turn's proposed state from an immutable snapshot and commit it only after validating the entire turn. Expand collective scopes into individual products before checking overlaps, allocation, component conflicts, eligibility and correction dependencies. An invalid aggregate must not leave an earlier valid row partially applied. Permuting independent rows must preserve the same state; explicit ordered corrections retain their order. A scoped permission withdrawal cannot remove a sibling product's refusal or unrelated valid facts. Failed or unknown note receipts cannot set a noted flag; persist unresolved effects and derive any terminal outcome from confirmed receipts and the supplied policy.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFor unfinished financial turns, persist complete components and use the component-specific recovery above instead of restarting the entire payment question or repeating a readiness cue. Include persistent sequence checks for complete offer acceptance without yes, pause then readiness, unfinished qualification then unconditional acceptance, and genuine unfinished amount then date-only speech. Assert the next spoken question, retained terms, bounded no-progress state, fresh readback and zero writes before later valid consent; a final ledger-only check misses the recovery loop. If the supplied policy permits no further clarification, use its truthful unresolved outcome rather than a fabricated agreement.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nKeep phase-specific security extraction simple and explicitly version-paired with the decoder. A supplied complete security answer must not disappear merely because its introductory wording changes. Distinguish missing/invalid extraction, unreadable format, an unfinished digit/year fragment, bank mismatch and explicit refusal; only a real completed bank comparison consumes a wrong-answer allowance. Never guess a missing phone digit or year or replace a bank verification receipt with local text recognition. Compile the exact required alternative channels and termination message for failed or declined security checks from the current brief; generic contact advice cannot silently replace specified app/branch directions. Before modifying a successful acknowledgement or mandatory opening disclosure in response to a judge verdict, compare the literal indexed API start/completion events and speech chronology; retain the original failed verdict and all mandatory source instructions.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Output contract\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nA security answer and an independent administrative question may share a single sentence or be separated by a comma, semicolon or coordinating clause. Extract the complete current requested answer and the question as separate acts from the same observed utterance; do not erase either act, infer unsupplied digits/year, or treat question wording as refusal. Answer allowed verification-purpose questions without account disclosure, then let only verify_identity establish backend validity. Preserve incomplete, quoted, negated, hypothetical and unrelated-subject exclusions; numbers in the independent question cannot supply missing security components. Pair literal complete-plus-question and partial-plus-question examples with the same producer/decoder version and persistent-store tests. If a clear current confirmation is observed but its typed event is absent, use the documented same-turn interpretation contract and a brief clarification; unknown extraction is not a new rejection or authority to write.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAn individual extraction variable's instructions must describe only that variable's scalar value. Separate event text, raw speech and administrative acts into their declared channels; instructions for an entire object envelope cannot be placed inside a scalar variable prompt. A strictly terminated event must end at its terminator with no appended keys, braces or sibling labels. Preserve whole-payload validation: do not repair a contaminated event by stripping an arbitrary suffix, ignoring malformed siblings or granting financial permission from raw model text. Keep current terms on malformed confirmation, distinguish extraction status from refusal, and follow the persisted current-question/readback recovery rule above; never alternate incompatible brief-confirmation and full-readback retries without tracking their context. Only a new valid current phase-bound affirmative can authorize writing. Count spoken per-product persuasion offers separately from refusal/exhaustion state transitions; obey the brief's treatment of an initial collective payment ask.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nNormalize word-year punctuation consistently before token counting and century composition. Support separately a complete century-plus-year expression and four explicitly spoken year digits; digit-by-digit years concatenate their supported digits rather than summing number words. Use the same completeness contract in fallback parsing and the missing-year question so a complete word-year cannot trigger a request to finish it. A conforming qualified canonical candidate follows the security-source rule above even if fallback normalization is unsupported; with no such candidate, unresolved expressions require clarification, never an additive or invented year. Keep day, month, year and phone grammars separate and retain incomplete operands. Paid and dispute dispositions must bind an actual current claim about returned bank products, with source subject and scope, quotation, negation and hypothetical qualifiers. Evaluate polarity for the claimed act: a policy-recognized denial of ownership such as not mine or never had is a positive dispute assertion, not a negated payment claim to reject through a shared blacklist. A denial of disputing does not assert a dispute. Resolve explicit self-corrections per target before selecting a disposition; a later denial of the same payment invalidates an earlier paid span, while refusing an additional payment or describing an unpaid sibling does not negate a supported current paid claim. A quoted note, diary, invoice, parcel or unrelated purchase cannot become a bank paid claim because a semantic row says paid. Missing or uncertain qualifying evidence requires neutral clarification, while genuine current-product claims and sibling proposals remain intact. Normalize supplied and observed self-identification punctuation symmetrically, preserving Unicode letters; separator or apostrophe variants cannot remove the current subject or override negative/quoted/third-party exclusions. Only documented runtime lifecycle hooks may finalize a customer disconnect; do not invent a hook, promise, receipt or successful close after a cutoff.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWrite only within the current run workdir. You may use shell/Python to generate and locally inspect JSON and snippets. Do not install packages, call network services, start other agents, modify kit files, inspect auth files or submit anything. The host owns Freya calls and official scoring. Finish with the required structured artifact paths and a brief honest summary. This is a real build; placeholder workflow graphs or hardcoded call transcripts are unacceptable.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nA mandatory guard that cannot execute must fail closed. Never add an LLM collection/write fallback in an outage to improve a practice score. Explicitly degraded enforcement is rejected by the host; preserve static safe exits and honest error states.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nTreat hosted extraction output as an independently tested producer contract. A declared primary variable may still be absent while raw speech and administrative fields are emitted. Inspect the saved structured extractor response and count primary-field coverage before attributing the failure to confidence, a missing schema field, or bank infrastructure. Keep the primary scalar description concise, with a single coherent grammar, phase-specific meanings, exact matching decoder examples and no sibling-variable envelope instructions. Each sibling description requests only its own value; preserve the built-in template unless a documented custom template includes every required speech, conversation, type and variable placeholder. A bounded validation retry may repair format, but is not permission to salvage missing financial consent from raw speech. Test the actual normalized published schema as well as the controller. Raw neutral identity facts require bank comparison; missing financial primary acts require bounded clarification and remain non-authoritative.\r\n\r\nReconcile aggregate monetary amounts in exact minor units or decimal arithmetic derived from the API precision. Binary floating-point equality must not reject a valid fractional total. On verified completion, including format exhaustion, retain every note obligation required by the supplied policy per returned product, with its supported reason and pending, successful, failed or unknown receipt state. A note succeeds only on its current documented successful bank receipt. Exhausting one note's policy retry budget must not discard or skip independent sibling obligations; process those still permitted before closure, preserving recorded promises and unresolved effects. Use the supplied terminal failure rule when a required effect remains failed or unknown; if it is unspecified, record that policy gap and use the permitted safe failure path without claiming the obligation was fulfilled or retrying indefinitely. Where the supplied policy forbids notes on transfer, defer and suppress those effects on that path while preserving recorded promises and cancelling unrecorded authorization. Never turn malformed proposals into payment/refusal authority.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFor paid/dispute dispositions, bind every resolved target to the positively asserted current bank claim. A claimed source span mentioning one product does not authorize expanding a model-supplied all-products or multi-product scope. Validate each target or an explicit genuine collective bank-products assertion; neutralize unsupported targets and preserve independent sibling terms. This guard applies to add_note as well as payment promises. Separate security-source qualification from value normalization. Require a current, unquoted, positive self-answer to the requested field with complete supported components and no unresolved correction or conflicting operand. Validate the extracted canonical answer against its advertised grammar and calendar, then submit that candidate unchanged to the bank; an unsupported wording in a narrower raw normalizer is not itself a source conflict. When raw normalization independently succeeds, disagreement requires clarification rather than silently replacing the candidate. Missing components, wrong subjects, quoted/negated answers and digits imported from other clauses remain vetoes even for well-formed canonical extraction. Normalize ordinary terminal punctuation and numeric separators without inventing a year or digit. Administrative flags are exact parsed tokens, never substring matches (a paid token contains letters ai but is not an AI question).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nA complete current requested security answer and a separate purpose/balance/AI question are concurrent acts. Reply to the allowed question under the current disclosure policy, preserve the complete answer candidate, and perform the mandatory bank comparison. A purpose keyword in raw speech cannot replace a conforming complete security frame with refusal or consume the security-attempt budget. Account-balance questions before verification receive a neutral privacy explanation, never debt disclosure. Only a genuine current answer refusal, unsupported subject, incomplete answer, or an actual failed bank comparison takes its corresponding path. Test canonical DOB plus purpose and balance questions separately from purpose-only, quoted dates and unfinished answers.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nApply target exclusions and negated target clauses before authorizing collective paid/dispute dispositions. An all-products or loans-only assertion with except, excluding, apart from, other than, or a contradictory named negative clause cannot authorize a note for the excluded target. An unfinished or ambiguous exclusion blocks the collective expansion. Preserve only positively supported targets and independent sibling decisions; never erase the exclusion by trusting the model's p=all scope. A canonical security-date candidate must agree with complete explicit self-answer evidence, including validated fragments retained for this same active security question and answer revision. For a split DOB, retain the supplied day and month while the complete year arrives; replace only an explicitly corrected component, and clear the whole buffer on an explicit whole-answer restart or a change of requested field. Submit only once all required components are complete, then explicitly clear consumed fragments before the next comparison attempt. Preserve fragments through missing extraction and unrelated questions without importing their numbers. Parse an actual complete explicit year, not merely a year-looking prefix; an incomplete or conflicting buffered answer requires clarification without a guessed comparison. Do not borrow components from an earlier completed or failed answer, another subject, an incidental question or a different security field.\r\n\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
